<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115263" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψᾰθῠρός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>friable, crumbling,</i>
			of the roe in fish, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				510b26
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰχθῦς . . τοὺς σαρκώδεις καὶ ψ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diocl.Fr.
					141
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλίσχρος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				387a15
			</span></i>; of bread, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.523
			</span></i>; of cheese, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κολλώδης,</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				698
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			); of meat, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				4.2.8
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὕδωρ ψ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Sens.</u>
					441a25
				</span></i>
			; of air, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>de An.</u>
				419b35
			</span></i>; of earth, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				2.4.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				145
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ -ωτέρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Gp.</u>
					3.3.10
				</span></i>
			; of the texture of some bulbs, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				7.9.4
			</span></i>; of leaves in a salad, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Liqu.</u>
				5
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			); also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψαδυρόν:</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσθενές, μαδαρόν, ψαθυρόν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (the form is 
				Att.
			 acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				16.760
			</span></i>), and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψαθαρά:</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔθλαστα,</span> etc., <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψαφαρός.</span></div>
